Fix shiboken internal error: Class "QByteArray" for
"QShaderCode::QShaderCode()" / "QRhiTextureSubresourceUploadDescription::QRhiTextureSubresourceUploadDescription()" not found.

The typesystem_gui_rhi.xml declares QShaderCode as a value-type with
private="yes".  Even though private types skip binding generation,
shiboken still tries to resolve constructor parameter types and
member variable types.  QShaderCode's constructor takes QByteArray
(and the class has QByteArray member variables), but the
load-typesystem chain from typesystem_gui.xml does not make
QByteArray visible in typesystem_gui_rhi.xml's resolution context.

Fix by demoting QShaderCode from <value-type> to <primitive-type>.
Primitive types are treated opaquely by shiboken — constructors and
member types are not resolved, so no QByteArray lookup is needed.
This is safe because:
- QShaderCode is private="yes" (no Python bindings generated)
- All types that reference QShaderCode in this file are also private
- The one external reference (typesystem_quick.xml) uses
  modify-function remove="all" which does not require full type info

--- a/sources/pyside6/PySide6/QtGui/typesystem_gui_rhi.xml
+++ b/sources/pyside6/PySide6/QtGui/typesystem_gui_rhi.xml
@@ -176,8 +176,8 @@
       <enum-type name="Variant"/>
       <enum-type name="SerializedFormatVersion"/>
   </value-type>
-  <value-type name="QShaderCode" since="6.6" private="yes"/>
+  <primitive-type name="QShaderCode"/>
   <value-type name="QShaderKey" since="6.6" private="yes"/>
   <value-type name="QShaderVersion" since="6.6" private="yes">
     <enum-type name="Flag" flags="Flags"/>
   </value-type>

--- a/sources/pyside6/PySide6/QtGui/typesystem_gui_rhi.xml
+++ b/sources/pyside6/PySide6/QtGui/typesystem_gui_rhi.xml
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@
   </value-type>
-  <value-type name="QRhiTextureSubresourceUploadDescription" since="6.6" private="yes"/>
+  <primitive-type name="QRhiTextureSubresourceUploadDescription"/>
   <value-type name="QRhiTextureUploadEntry" since="6.6" private="yes"/>
   <value-type name="QRhiTextureUploadDescription" since="6.6" private="yes">
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@
   <value-type name="QRhiTextureCopyDescription" since="6.6" private="yes"/>
-  <value-type name="QRhiReadbackDescription" since="6.6" private="yes"/>
+  <primitive-type name="QRhiReadbackDescription"/>
   <value-type name="QRhiNativeHandles" since="6.6" private="yes"/>
